          "title": "Master Formula Table (Unit 1)",
          "markdown": "## 3. Master Formula Table (Unit 1)\n\n| Quantity | Formula | SI Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Thin-film optical path difference (reflected) | $\\Delta = 2\\mu t \\cos r \\pm \\frac{\\lambda}{2}$ | $\\text{m}$ |\n| Wedge fringe width | $\\beta = \\frac{\\lambda}{2\\mu\\theta}$ | $\\text{m}$ ($\\theta$ in $\\text{rad}$) |\n| Newton's $n^{\\text{th}}$ dark ring diameter | $D_n^2 = 4n\\lambda R$ | $\\text{m}^2$ |\n| Newton's $n^{\\text{th}}$ bright ring diameter | $D_n^2 = 2(2n - 1)\\lambda R$ | $\\text{m}^2$ |\n| Wavelength & liquid index (Newton's rings) | $\\lambda = \\frac{D_{n+p}^2 - D_n^2}{4pR}$, $\\mu = \\frac{(\\Delta D^2)_{\\text{air}}}{(\\Delta D^2)_{\\text{liq}}}$ | $\\lambda$ in $\\text{m}$, $\\mu$ dimensionless |\n| Michelson interferometer displacement | $2d = N\\lambda$ | $\\text{m}$ |\n| Single slit minima & central width | $a\\sin\\theta = m\\lambda$, $2\\theta_1 = \\frac{2\\lambda}{a}$, $W = \\frac{2\\lambda f}{a}$ | $\\theta$ in $\\text{rad}$, $W$ in $\\text{m}$ |\n| Diffraction grating principal maxima | $(a+b)\\sin\\theta = n\\lambda$ | $\\text{m}$ |\n| Telescope resolving limit & RP | $d\\theta = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D}$, $\\text{RP} = \\frac{D}{1.22\\lambda}$ | $\\text{rad}$, $\\text{rad}^{-1}$ |\n| Grating resolving power | $\\text{RP} = \\frac{\\lambda}{d\\lambda} = nN$ | Dimensionless |\n| Quarter- & half-wave plate | $t_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4|\\mu_o - \\mu_e|}$, $t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2|\\mu_o - \\mu_e|}$ | $\\text{m}$ |"
