          "title": "Common Mistakes Checklist",
          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Confusing **interference** and **diffraction** formulas: $a\\sin\\theta = m\\lambda$ gives **minima** in a single slit, whereas $(a+b)\\sin\\theta = n\\lambda$ gives **maxima** in a grating!\n* Plugging radius $r$ instead of diameter $D$ into $D_n^2 = 4n\\lambda R$ (the radius formula is $r_n^2 = n\\lambda R$, factor $1$ not $4$).\n* Mixing up **inch vs meter** conversion in grating problems: $1\\text{ inch} = 2.54\\text{ cm} = 0.0254\\text{ m}$, so grating element $e = \\frac{0.0254}{\\text{lines/inch}}$.\n* Forgetting the **factor of $2$** in Michelson interferometer ($2d = N\\lambda$, because light goes forward and returns).\n* Writing $\\theta_1 = \\lambda/a$ as the *total* angular width instead of the *half-width*—total angular width of the central maximum is **$2\\lambda/a$**."
