          "id": "ch-5-exam-questions-with-complete-answers",
          "number": "5",
          "title": "Exam Questions (With Complete Answers)",
          "markdown": "## 5. Exam Questions (With Complete Answers)\n\n### Short Answer Questions (2 Marks Each)\n\n1. **Define population inversion and metastable state.**\n   **Answer:** *Population inversion* is the non-equilibrium state where more atoms occupy an upper excited level than a lower level ($N_2 > N_1$). A *metastable state* is an excited level with an unusually long lifetime ($\\sim 10^{-3}\\text{ s}$ instead of $10^{-8}\\text{ s}$), allowing atoms to accumulate for laser action.\n2. **State any two ways He-Ne laser is superior to Ruby laser.**\n   **Answer:** (i) He-Ne gives a **continuous wave (CW)** output (Ruby is pulsed); (ii) being a 4-level system, it needs far lower pumping power and produces superior **monochromaticity and beam stability**.\n3. **Why is modal dispersion negligible in a single-mode step-index fibre?**\n   **Answer:** Because only **one axial mode** propagates ($V < 2.405$), all light energy travels along nearly a single path at the same group velocity, eliminating pulse broadening caused by multi-path arrival delays.\n4. **Compare step-index and graded-index (GRIN) multimode fibres.**\n   **Answer:** Step-index has a uniform core index $n_1$ (abrupt jump to $n_2$ at cladding), straight zig-zag ray paths, and high modal dispersion. GRIN has a parabolically decreasing core index $n(r)$, sinusoidal ray paths, and very low modal dispersion.\n5. **Write two advantages of optical fibre communication over copper cables.** *(BEU Mid-Sem 2026)*\n   **Answer:** Complete immunity to electromagnetic interference (EMI)/crosstalk and vastly wider signal bandwidth (THz) with low attenuation ($\\sim 0.2\\text{ dB/km}$ at $1550\\text{ nm}$).\n\n### Long Answer Questions (7–10 Marks Each)\n\n1. **What are Einstein's $A$ and $B$ coefficients? Derive the relation between them ($B_{12}=B_{21}$ and $A_{21}/B_{21} = 8\\pi h\\nu^3/c^3$).** *(Follow Derivation §2.2 step-by-step from Boltzmann equilibrium to Planck's radiation comparison.)*\n2. **Draw a neat labeled diagram of the He-Ne laser (or Ruby laser) and explain its construction and energy-level working mechanism.** *(Use the Ruby & He-Ne Lasers diagram above + Table §2.3: $10:1$ He:Ne discharge $\\to$ He $2^1S_0/2^3S_1$ resonant transfer to Ne $3s/2s \\to$ $632.8\\text{ nm}$ lasing to Ne $2p \\to 1s \\to$ tube wall.)*\n3. **Derive expressions for the acceptance angle ($\\theta_a$) and Numerical Aperture (NA) of a step-index optical fibre. Discuss attenuation losses in fibres.** *(Use the Optical Fibre & Acceptance Cone diagram above + §2.4 & §2.5.)*"
