          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Writing $\\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}(n_1/n_2)$ instead of $\\sin^{-1}(n_2/n_1)$: since $n_1 > n_2$, $n_1/n_2 > 1$ has **no inverse sine**!\n* Confusing **radius $a$** with **diameter $d = 2a$** in $V = \\frac{2\\pi a}{\\lambda}\\text{NA} = \\frac{\\pi d}{\\lambda}\\text{NA}$.\n* Using natural log $\\ln$ instead of base-10 $\\log_{10}$ in $\\alpha = \\frac{10}{L}\\log_{10}(P_{\\text{in}}/P_{\\text{out}})$.\n* Stating Helium is the lasing gas in He-Ne: **Helium is only the pumping helper**; **Neon** emits the $632.8\\text{ nm}$ laser beam!\n* Forgetting $n_0$ when light launches from **water ($n_0 = 1.33$)** instead of air: $\\sin\\theta_a = \\frac{\\text{NA}}{n_0}$, whereas $\\text{NA} = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2}$ stays unchanged!"
