          "title": "Master Formula Table (Unit 3)",
          "markdown": "## 3. Master Formula Table (Unit 3)\n\n| Quantity | Formula | SI Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Electric displacement vector | $\\vec{D} = \\epsilon_0\\vec{E} + \\vec{P} = \\epsilon_0\\epsilon_r\\vec{E}$ | $\\text{C/m}^2$ |\n| Capacitor with dielectric | $C = \\frac{\\epsilon_0\\epsilon_r A}{d}$, $U = \\frac{1}{2}CV^2$ | $\\text{F}$, $\\text{J}$ |\n| Magnetization & permeability | $\\vec{B} = \\mu_0(\\vec{H} + \\vec{M}) = \\mu_0\\mu_r\\vec{H}$, $\\mu_r = 1 + \\chi_m$ | $\\vec{B}$ in $\\text{T}$, $\\vec{H}, \\vec{M}$ in $\\text{A/m}$ |\n| Displacement current density | $\\vec{J}_d = \\frac{\\partial\\vec{D}}{\\partial t} = \\epsilon\\frac{\\partial\\vec{E}}{\\partial t}$ | $\\text{A/m}^2$ |\n| Continuity equation | $\\nabla\\cdot\\vec{J}_c + \\frac{\\partial\\rho}{\\partial t} = 0$ | $\\text{A/m}^3$ |\n| Wave speed & impedance (vacuum) | $c = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mu_0\\epsilon_0}} \\approx 3\\times 10^8$, $\\eta_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mu_0}{\\epsilon_0}} \\approx 377$ | $\\text{m/s}$, $\\Omega$ |\n| Poynting vector & average intensity | $\\vec{S} = \\vec{E}\\times\\vec{H}$, $\\langle S\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2}E_0 H_0 = \\frac{E_0^2}{2\\eta_0} = \\frac{P}{4\\pi r^2}$ | $\\text{W/m}^2$ |\n| Skin depth in good conductor | $\\delta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi f \\mu \\sigma}}$ | $\\text{m}$ |"
