          "id": "ch-4-solved-numericals-6-problems",
          "number": "4",
          "title": "Solved Numericals (6 Problems)",
          "markdown": "## 4. Solved Numericals (6 Problems)\n\n### Problem 1 (Dielectric Capacitor: $E$, $D$, $P$, $C$)\nA parallel-plate capacitor ($A = 100\\text{ cm}^2$, $d = 1\\text{ mm}$) is filled with a dielectric of $\\epsilon_r = 5$ and connected to a $100\\text{ V}$ supply. Find: (a) electric field $E$, (b) displacement $D$, (c) polarization $P$, and (d) capacitance $C$.\n\n**Solution:**\n**(a)** $E = \\frac{V}{d} = \\frac{100}{10^{-3}} = \\mathbf{1.0 \\times 10^5\\text{ V/m}}$.\n**(b)** $D = \\epsilon_0\\epsilon_r E = 8.854 \\times 10^{-12} \\times 5 \\times 10^5 = \\mathbf{4.427\\ \\mu\\text{C/m}^2}$.\n**(c)** $P = \\epsilon_0(\\epsilon_r - 1)E = 8.854 \\times 10^{-12} \\times 4 \\times 10^5 = \\mathbf{3.542\\ \\mu\\text{C/m}^2}$.\n**(d)** $C = \\frac{\\epsilon_0\\epsilon_r A}{d} = \\frac{8.854 \\times 10^{-12} \\times 5 \\times 10^{-2}}{10^{-3}} = \\mathbf{0.4427\\text{ nF}}$.\n\n---\n\n### Problem 2 (Magnetic Susceptibility, Flux Density & Magnetization)\nA magnetic material with relative permeability $\\mu_r = 500$ is placed in a magnetizing field $H = 200\\text{ A/m}$. Find $\\chi_m$, $B$, and $M$.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. $\\chi_m = \\mu_r - 1 = 500 - 1 = \\mathbf{499}$.\n2. $B = \\mu_0\\mu_r H = (4\\pi \\times 10^{-7}) \\times 500 \\times 200 = \\mathbf{0.1257\\text{ T}}$.\n3. $M = \\chi_m H = 499 \\times 200 = \\mathbf{99{,}800\\text{ A/m}}$.\n\n---\n\n### Problem 3 (Conduction vs Displacement Current Density)\nFind the conduction current density $J_c$ and displacement current density $J_d$ in a solid with $\\sigma = 10^{-3}\\text{ S/m}$ and $\\epsilon_r = 2.5$ when $E = 4.5 \\times 10^{-6}\\sin(10^9 t)\\text{ V/m}$.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. Conduction current density:\n   $$J_c = \\sigma E = 10^{-3} \\times 4.5 \\times 10^{-6}\\sin(10^9 t) = \\mathbf{4.50 \\times 10^{-9}\\sin(10^9 t)\\text{ A/m}^2}$$\n2. Displacement current density:\n   $$J_d = \\epsilon_0\\epsilon_r \\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial t} = (8.854 \\times 10^{-12})(2.5)(4.5 \\times 10^{-6})(10^9)\\cos(10^9 t) = \\mathbf{9.961 \\times 10^{-8}\\cos(10^9 t)\\text{ A/m}^2}$$\n\n---\n\n### Problem 4 (Poynting Intensity & Fields from a Lamp)\nA $100\\text{ W}$ sodium lamp radiates isotropically. Calculate the electric field ($E_0$) and magnetic field ($H_0, B_0$) peak strengths at $r = 5\\text{ m}$ from the lamp.\n\n**Solution:**\n1. Average power flux density (Poynting magnitude):\n   $$\\langle S \\rangle = \\frac{P}{4\\pi r^2} = \\frac{100}{4\\pi(5)^2} = \\frac{1}{\\pi} = \\mathbf{0.3183\\text{ W/m}^2}$$\n2. Peak electric field (using $\\eta_0 = 376.73\\ \\Omega$):\n   $$E_0 = \\sqrt{2\\eta_0 \\langle S \\rangle} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 376.73 \\times 0.3183} = \\mathbf{15.487\\text{ V/m}} \\quad (E_{\\text{rms}} = E_0/\\sqrt{2} = 10.95\\text{ V/m})$$\n3. Peak magnetic field:\n   $$H_0 = \\frac{E_0}{\\eta_0} = \\mathbf{0.0411\\text{ A/m}}, \\qquad B_0 = \\frac{E_0}{c} = \\frac{15.487}{3 \\times 10^8} = \\mathbf{51.62\\text{ nT}}$$\n\n---\n\n### Problem 5 (Solar Constant Field Strengths)\nSunlight hits Earth's upper atmosphere with energy flux $\\langle S \\rangle = 1.38\\text{ kW/m}^2 = 1380\\text{ W/m}^2$. Find peak values $E_0$ and $B_0$.\n\n**Solution:**\n$$E_0 = \\sqrt{2\\eta_0 \\langle S \\rangle} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 376.73 \\times 1380} = \\mathbf{1019.7\\text{ V/m}}$$\n$$B_0 = \\frac{E_0}{c} = \\frac{1019.7}{3 \\times 10^8} = \\mathbf{3.399\\ \\mu\\text{T}}$$\n\n---\n\n### Problem 6 (Skin Depth in Aluminum)\nFind the skin depth $\\delta$ at frequency $f = 1.6\\text{ MHz}$ in aluminum ($\\sigma = 38.2 \\times 10^6\\text{ S/m}$, $\\mu_r = 1$).\n\n**Solution:**\n$$\\delta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi f \\mu_0 \\mu_r \\sigma}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi (1.6 \\times 10^6)(4\\pi \\times 10^{-7})(1)(38.2 \\times 10^6)}} = \\mathbf{64.38\\ \\mu\\text{m}}$$"
