          "markdown": "## 6. Common Mistakes Checklist\n* Confusing **rms** ($E_{\\text{rms}}$) and **peak** ($E_0$) values in lamp Poynting problems: $\\langle S\\rangle = E_{\\text{rms}}^2/\\eta_0 = \\mathbf{\\frac{1}{2}}E_0^2/\\eta_0$ (do not drop the factor of $2$!).\n* Confusing $\\vec{H}$ ($\\text{A/m}$) and $\\vec{B}$ ($\\text{T} = \\text{Wb/m}^2$): $\\vec{B} = \\mu_0\\vec{H}$ in vacuum, and $\\vec{S} = \\vec{E}\\times\\vec{H} = \\frac{1}{\\mu_0}(\\vec{E}\\times\\vec{B})$.\n* Forgetting to square $r$ or multiply by $4\\pi$ in spherical lamp radiation: $\\langle S\\rangle = \\frac{P}{4\\pi r^2}$.\n* Using degrees/wrong frequency conversion ($1\\text{ MHz} = 10^6\\text{ Hz}$) or forgetting $A$ conversion ($100\\text{ cm}^2 = 10^{-2}\\text{ m}^2$, NOT $10^{-4}$).\n* Saying Curie's law ($\\chi_m = C/T$) applies to ferromagnets below $T_C$: above $T_C$ a ferromagnet becomes paramagnetic obeying **Curie-Weiss law** $\\chi_m = C/(T - T_C)$."
